o proposed\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e796; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e1013 [party_statement; finance.biggo.com; original source Amazon ; from gnews:bca40137e0cfa49b30e5b0f7 2026-10-03] Amazon tells investors that each generation of semiconductors has a useful life of at least five years, and that starting in 2025 it shortened the useful life of certain server and networking equipment from six years to five years.\n    Quote: Amazon tells investors that each generation of semiconductors has a useful life of at least five years. Starting in 2025, the company also shortened the useful life of certain server and networking equipment from six years to five years.\n- e1017 [rumour; finance.biggo.com; original source Unnamed lenders (reported) ; from gnews:01dc582fbe53203eaeac2c61 2026-10-03] The article reports, without naming the lenders or citing a source, that some lenders involved in Nvidia's AI infrastructure financing plan are seeking stronger collateral than the company originally outlined, as they try to calculate how long chip revenue will be sustainable.\n    Quote: However, Nvidia's ambitious financing plan has sparked debate on Wall Street about the real value of its advanced chips and associated infrastructure. Some lenders are seeking stronger collateral than originally outlined by the company, even given its industry-leading processing power, as they try to calculate how long chip revenue will be sustainable.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e961; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e1034 [rumour; bhaskarenglish.in (citing unnamed banking sources and credit managers); original source  ; from gnews:4588a36d112063025acf1bb1 2026-10-03] According to unnamed banking sources and credit managers, some lenders are demanding substantial guarantees from NVIDIA against the value of its advanced chips and infrastructure, and are assessing how long