er gigawatt for Grace Blackwell and roughly $40 billion per gigawatt for Vera Rubin.\n    Quote: Grace Blackwell is already one generation behind Vera Rubin. NVIDIA says Vera Rubin delivers 35X lower token costs than Grace Blackwell Ultra. NVIDIA estimates about $25 billion per gigawatt of revenue for Grace Blackwell and roughly $40 billion for Vera Rubin.\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e117; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e1047 [party_statement; Yahoo Finance; original source Amazon (Andy Jassy) ; from gnews:ed14a9d1371ea43f3c5dcd3d 2026-10-04] Amazon CEO Andy Jassy said on the July earnings call that servers take \"a little less than three years\" to break even and last at least five to six years.\n    Quote: On the July earnings call, Jassy said servers take \"a little less than three years\" to break even and last at least five to six years.\n- e1049 [fact; Yahoo Finance; original source NVIDIA ; from gnews:ed14a9d1371ea43f3c5dcd3d 2026-10-04] NVIDIA is building financing structures similar to Amazon's sale-leaseback and signed up six asset managers and banks to raise more than $500 billion of outside capital for AI infrastructure; management said: \"We know some will call this circular financing.\"\n    Quote: NVIDIA is building similar structures. … It signed up six asset managers and banks to raise more than $500 billion of outside capital for AI infrastructure. Management said: \"We know some will call this circular financing.\"\n    Opinion, not verified: the matcher read this as the same claim as e796; the argument counts one claim, one more outlet.\n- e1129 [fact; Morningstar; original source Nvidia ; from gnews:62b41f9768d1b65460f326ca 2026-10-05] Nvidia has pledged $500 billion to its partnership with Apollo Global Management, BlackRock, Blackstone, Brookfield, Goldman Sachs and KKR, aimed at supporting enterprises such as AI laboratories, cloud storage providers and data-center operators that 